steps:
Step 4 — StudioGettingStarted.tsx: transform the flat list into a styled step checklist. In the JSX, wrap each <li> in a div with className='getting-started-step'. Add an icon area before the step text — use a small numbered badge. Change the <ol> className from 'list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2' to 'getting-started-steps'. Add the service readiness grid styling. Define new CSS in crm-studio.css:
  .getting-started-steps { list-style:none; padding:0; margin:0; display:grid; gap:12px; }
  .getting-started-step { display:flex; align-items:flex-start; gap:14px; padding:14px 16px; border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:12px; background:var(--card); transition:background .15s ease-out; }
  .getting-started-step:hover { background:var(--purple-50); }
  .step-number { flex-shrink:0; width:26px; height:26px; border-radius:50%; background:var(--purple-100); color:var(--purple-700); display:grid; place-items:center; font:700 11px 'DM Mono',monospace; }
  .service-status-grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(180px,1fr)); gap:12px; }
  .service-status-card { padding:14px 16px; border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:12px; background:var(--card); }
  .service-status-card strong { display:block; font-size:13px; margin-bottom:4px; }
  .service-ready { color:var(--green-500); } .service-unavailable { color:var(--rose-500); }
  In StudioGettingStarted.tsx: replace the <ol className='list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2'> block with a <ol className='getting-started-steps'>. Inside each <li>, wrap content with <div className='getting-started-step'><span className='step-number'>{index+1}</span><span>{li content}</span></div>. Since the steps are static text items, do this by converting the <li>text</li> items to JSX with an explicit step-number span. Replace the .studio-grid aria-live='polite' section with .service-status-grid and each child div with .service-status-card, coloring the ready/unavailable text with .service-ready/.service-unavailable classes.
